# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored - never commit real values.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle,
# so everything here is PUBLIC and readable by anyone. Never a private API key,
# a JWT secret or an SMTP credential - those live in server/.env, which has no
# VITE_ prefix precisely so they cannot be inlined by accident.
#
# There is currently nothing the public bundle needs.
#
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT / VITE_FORM_ACCESS_KEY were removed in Phase 1c. The enquiry
# form posts to this site's own API at /api/enquiries, so there is no third-party
# form provider in the path any more. Submissions are stored in Postgres and shown
# under Enquiries in the admin; the notification email is configured server-side
# (SMTP_*, NOTIFY_EMAIL in server/.env.example).


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DOCKER COMPOSE - staging deploy (docker-compose.yml)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Everything above concerns the Vite build and is still accurate: the public
# bundle needs no variables. Everything BELOW is read by docker-compose.yml,
# which substitutes from a `.env` file sitting beside it.
#
#     cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must stay so - it holds the database password, the
# JWT signing key and the first admin's credentials. None of these carry a VITE_
# prefix, and none ever may: VITE_* is inlined into public JavaScript.
#
# server/.env is NOT used by the containers. Compose passes these values in as
# environment variables directly, so server/.env stays a local-development file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- database --
# Composed into DATABASE_URL for the `api` and `seed` services. Postgres is
# never published to a host port, so this is only reachable from inside the
# stack's internal network.
POSTGRES_USER=solstice
POSTGRES_DB=solstice
# Generate:  openssl rand -base64 24
# Avoid characters that need URL-encoding in a connection string - @ : / ? #
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- auth ------
# Signs admin session tokens. Rotating it logs every admin out immediately.
# Generate:  openssl rand -hex 48
JWT_SECRET=
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=12h

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- CORS ------
# main.ts splits on commas and refuses "*" by design, because the API issues
# credentials. Do NOT add a production origin - this stack must never serve
# solsticellp.com.
CORS_ORIGIN=https://test.solsticellp.com,https://test-api.solsticellp.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- seeding ---
# Read ONLY by prisma/seed.ts, which throws if either is missing. Together they
# create the single first admin - the login for
# https://test.solsticellp.com/#admin
#
# After that the seed finds an existing admin row and leaves it untouched, so
# editing these later changes nothing. Change the password in the admin UI.
ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL=
# Long, please. bcrypt-hashed at cost 12 on first seed.
ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mail ------
# Optional. If SMTP_HOST is blank the API logs a warning at boot and skips the
# notification; the enquiry is still saved and still appears in the admin, so
# nothing is lost while this is unconfigured.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM=Solstice website <no-reply@solsticetrading.com>
NOTIFY_EMAIL=
